(a) the progress made under Mission LiFE in promoting sustainable lifestyles across the country;
(b) the number of States, educational institutions and local bodies participating in the programme;
(c) whether measurable indicators have been developed to assess behavioural changes and environmental outcomes;
(d) the budgetary allocations made for Mission LiFE during the current financial year; and
(e) the steps being taken to enhance public participation in climate action?

(a) whether Government has granted licences or spectrum authorisations for satellite-based internet services in the country;
(b) the details of companies permitted to provide such services;
(c) the manner in which satellite broadband is proposed to complement BharatNet and terrestrial telecom networks, particularly in remote and difficult areas; and
(d) the safeguards put in place regarding affordability, security and spectrum management for satellite communication services?

(a) whether Government has commenced implementation of the Multi-Lane Free Flow (MLFF) toll collection system on National Highways;
(b) the details of highways and toll plazas where the system has been operationalised or approved;
(c) the expected timeline for nationwide implementation of the barrier-less tolling system; and
(d) the measures taken to address issues relating to incorrect toll deductions, grievance redressal and data privacy of road users?

(a) whether Government has assessed the availability and timely supply of subsidised fertilizers, including urea, DAP, NPK and other major ones to farmers during the current agricultural season;
(b) if so, the details thereof including  State-wise requirement, allocation and supply of fertilizers during the current season with special reference to Kerala;
(c) whether any shortages or delays in fertilizer supply have been reported during the last two years and the reasons therefor; and
(d) the measures taken to ensure adequate availability of fertilizers at affordable and notified prices and prevent black marketing and diversion?

(a) whether Government has prepared a roadmap to enhance India's petroleum refining capacity by 2030;
(b) the details of new refinery and petrochemical projects under implementation;
(c) the expected increase in domestic refining capacity and petrochemical production; and
(d) the manner in which these projects will reduce import dependence and strengthen India's energy security?

(a) the present status of the National River Interlinking Programme;
(b) the river-linking projects approved or under implementation during the last three years;
(c) the estimated irrigation, drinking water and hydropower benefits expected from these projects; and
(d) the steps taken to address environmental concerns and ensure rehabilitation of affected families?

(a) the progress achieved under the Deendayal Antyodaya Yojana–National Rural Livelihoods Mission (DAY-NRLM) during the last three years;
(b) the number of Self-Help Groups (SHGs) formed, women beneficiaries covered and credit linked under the Mission;
(c) whether Government proposes to enhance market access and digital marketing support for SHGs; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has initiated the development of thematic tourism trails, including the Bird Watching Trail at Pulicat Lake and the Eco and Nature Trail at Podhigai Hills in Tamil Nadu;
(b) the details of funds allocated and released for these projects;
(c) the expected timeline for their completion; and
(d) the measures taken to ensure local community participation and sustainable tourism practices in these destinations?

(a) the present status of implementation of Mission Shakti, including operationalisation of One Stop Centres (OSCs) across the country;
(b) the number of OSCs sanctioned, operational and pending, State-wise;
(c) whether Government proposes to enhance staffing, rehabilitation services and support for women migrating for employment under the scheme; and
(d) the steps taken to improve monitoring and service delivery at the district level?

(a) whether Government proposes to enhance investment in health research and disease surveillance infrastructure;
(b) the present status of strengthening viral diagnostic laboratories, multidisciplinary research units and model rural health research units;
(c) the steps taken to fill vacancies in research institutions under the Indian Council of Medical Research (ICMR); and
(d) the budgetary allocation made for health research during 2026-27 and the expected outcomes?

(a) whether India recently hosted the first BRICS MSME forum;
(b) the major outcomes and recommendations emerging from the forum;
(c) the initiatives proposed to strengthen international cooperation, innovation, exports and technology transfer among BRICS countries; and
(d) the manner in which Indian MSMEs are expected to benefit from these collaborations?

(a) whether Government has conducted any recent assessment of groundwater levels across the country;
(b) the number of over-exploited, critical and semi-critical groundwater blocks, State-wise;
(c) the measures being implemented to promote groundwater recharge and rainwater harvesting; and
(d) whether any special assistance is being provided to water-stressed States to address groundwater depletion?

(a) whether Government has commenced implementation of the Export Promotion Mission (EPM) to strengthen India's export ecosystem;
(b) the total financial outlay and key components of the Mission;
(c) the measures proposed to support MSMEs, first-time exporters and exporters from aspirational districts; and
(d) the expected impact of the Mission on India's merchandise and services exports and employment generation?

(a) whether Government has launched Mission for Aatmanirbharta in Pulses to reduce dependence on imports;
(b) the targets fixed for increasing domestic pulses production;
(c) the support proposed for pulse growers through procurement, storage and processing facilities; and
(d) the expected impact of the Mission on farmers' income and national food security?

(a) whether the Ministry has recently reviewed the infrastructure projects proposed within or adjoining tiger reserves and other protected areas;
(b) the criteria adopted by the Expert Appraisal Committee while considering such proposals;
(c) the number of projects modified, deferred or rejected during the last two years;
(d) the safeguards prescribed to minimise ecological damage; and
(e) whether Government proposes to strengthen environmental appraisal procedures for ecologically sensitive landscapes?

(a) whether Government has taken note of the reported rise in POCSO and sexual assault cases in various States, including Tamil Nadu;
(b) the State-wise number of such cases registered, charge-sheeted and resulting in convictions during the last three years;
(c) the measures taken to strengthen investigation, fast-track courts, forensic support and victim rehabilitation; and
(d) whether Government proposes to provide additional assistance to States to improve women's and children's safety and ensure timely justice?

(a) whether Tamil Nadu has received Central assistance under the Ayushman Bharat–Pradhan Mantri Jan Arogya Yojana (AB-PMJAY) despite implementing its own Chief Minister's Comprehensive Health Insurance Scheme (CMCHIS);
(b) the details of funds allocated and released to the State during the last three years;
(c) whether any proposals for convergence or integration of the two schemes are under consideration; and
(d) the steps taken to ensure that eligible beneficiaries in Tamil Nadu receive adequate Central support for health insurance coverage?

(a) view of Cauvery Water Management Authority (CWMA) regarding the release of Cauvery water to the State of Tamil Nadu;
(b) whether the prescribed monthly water releases have been complied with during the last three years;
(c) the details of instances of shortfall, if any, and the action taken thereon; and
(d) the measures proposed to ensure timely release of Tamil Nadu's allocated share in accordance with the orders of the competent authorities?

(a) whether it is a fact that the Ministry is considering the introduction of a Vande Bharat Express train connecting Madurai and Coimbatore in both directions;
(b) if so, the present status and the expected timeline for its introduction; and
(c) if not, whether Government will consider introducing a Vande Bharat Express service between Madurai and Coimbatore, in view of the growing passenger demand, tourism, educational institutions and industrial connectivity between the two cities?

(a) whether Government has launched any new initiative for eco-restoration of degraded forest lands under its Green India Mission;
(b) the total area identified and restored during the last three years, State-wise, including Tamil Nadu;
(c) the funds allocated and utilised therefor; and
(d) the measures taken to ensure community participation and improve biodiversity through such restoration efforts?

(a) whether Government has reviewed the recent trends in formal employment generation based on EPFO and ESIC enrolment data; 
(b) the sector-wise and State-wise increase in formal employment during the last three years; 
(c) whether any decline has been observed in employment generation in specific sectors; and 
(d) the corrective measures taken to accelerate formal job creation, particularly for youth and women?

(a) whether Government has undertaken a review of the implementation of Mission Vatsalya and child protection services;
(b) the steps taken to identify and regulate unregistered child care institutions across the country;
(c) whether Government proposes to undertake a national audit of child care institutions and strengthen inter-State child repatriation mechanisms; and
(d) the measures taken to fill vacancies in child protection institutions and improve rehabilitation services for vulnerable children?

(a) the steps taken to promote Intelligent Transport Systems (ITS), Artificial Intelligence-based traffic management and digital monitoring on National Highways;
(b) whether Government has assessed the impact of these technologies on reducing travel time, congestion and fuel consumption;
(c) the details of expenditure incurred on deployment of such technologies during the last three years; and
(d) the roadmap for expanding technology-enabled highway infrastructure across the country?

(a) the progress made under the Ayushman Bharat Digital Mission (ABDM) with regard to creation of digital health IDs, registration of health facilities and healthcare professionals;
(b) the measures taken to strengthen interoperability, cyber security and protection of patients' health data;
(c) whether telemedicine services have expanded in rural and remote areas under the Mission; and
(d) the details thereof, State-wise?

(a) whether the Central Government has formulated any comprehensive strategy to strengthen flood management and urban drainage systems in view of increasing instances of extreme rainfall, especially in Chennai;
(b) the funds released to States under flood management and anti-erosion schemes during the last three years;
(c) whether any flood forecasting and early warning systems have been upgraded using modern technologies; and
(d) the measures being taken in coordination with State Governments to minimise loss of life and property due to floods?

(a) whether Government has formulated any policy or incentive scheme to encourage the adoption of green and renewable energy, including solar and wind power, at airports across the country;
(b) the number of airports currently meeting a significant proportion of their energy requirements through renewable sources, State-wise;
(c) whether financial or technical assistance is being provided to Airports Authority of India and private airport operators for installation of renewable energy infrastructure; and
(d) the steps being taken to achieve carbon-neutral and energy-efficient airports in line with India's climate commitments?
